Intuition
If two indices are connected through allowedSwaps, we can rearrange elements among them freely (since swaps can be chained and repeated). This is a classic connected components problem — indices in the same component can share their elements in any order. So within each component, we just need to check how many source values can match target values.

Approach
Use Union-Find (DSU) to group indices that are connected via allowedSwaps.
For each connected component, collect all source values into a frequency map.
For each index in the component, check if target[i] exists in the frequency map. If yes, it's a match — decrement its count. If no, it contributes to Hamming distance.
This works because within a component we can freely rearrange source elements, so we greedily match as many as possible.

Complexity
Time complexity: O(n + m · α(n)) where m = number of allowed swaps and α is the inverse Ackermann function (nearly O(1)) from Union-Find
Space complexity: O(n) for the parent array and frequency maps

Code:-
class Solution {
    private int[] parent;

    private int find(int x) {
        if (parent[x] != x) parent[x] = find(parent[x]);
        return parent[x];
    }

    private void unite(int a, int b) {
        parent[find(a)] = find(b);
    }

    public int minimumHammingDistance(int[] source, int[] target, int[][] allowedSwaps) {
        int n = source.length;
        parent = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) parent[i] = i;

        for (int[] swap : allowedSwaps) {
            unite(swap[0], swap[1]);
        }

        // Group source values by their component root
        Map<Integer, Map<Integer, Integer>> groups = new HashMap<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int root = find(i);
            groups.computeIfAbsent(root, k -> new HashMap<>())
                  .merge(source[i], 1, Integer::sum);
        }

        int hammingDist = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int root = find(i);
            Map<Integer, Integer> freq = groups.get(root);
            if (freq.getOrDefault(target[i], 0) > 0) {
                freq.merge(target[i], -1, Integer::sum); // matched, consume this source value
            } else {
                hammingDist++;                           // no match found in this component
            }
        }

        return hammingDist;
    }
}
